title: ActFourNotes
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
style: note
---
Act IV, the day of the fair. The village again, with the fair, a child scene the story loads while $fair_up is true (the cartographer does not move: the stalls and the hearing table are simply there). The steward's figure stands at the fair and the village's is hidden: the same actor never shows twice. Speak for the mill only if the cartographer took a side on the road; Lio's first map only if Lio was not blamed. The hearing gives one of six endings. #line:ActFourNotes_0100
===

title: Events
act: Fair
location: Village
scenario: The hearing
quest: border
when: once
when: $act == Act.Fair
when: here() == "Village"
---
Ashcombe is full. Stalls on the green, flags over the bridge, and half the abbey in grey robes. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Fair_0100
At the far end of the green, a long table: the hearing, at noon. The Countess, the Prior, and an empty chair for the cartographer. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Fair_0200
<<if $jory_found>>
    Jory is at the front of the crowd, on a crutch, waving at you. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Fair_0300
<<endif>>
<<set $quest_border to QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed border>>
===

title: Bram
act: Fair
location: Village
scenario: The road
quest: mill
when: $act == Act.Fair
when: $quest_mill == QuestState.NotStarted and ($road == Road.Corvin or $road == Road.Miller)
---
<<if $road == Road.Miller>>
    Bram: You said it yourself. The road goes around the mill. Will you say it again, at the table, in front of the steward? #line:Bram.a487b07e_0100_Bram
<<else>>
    Bram: You sided with the steward, I know. But you've seen the mill now. Will you speak for us at the table? #line:Bram.a487b07e_0200_Bram
<<endif>>
-> I will speak for the mill. #line:Bram.a487b07e_0300
    Bram: That's all I ask. #line:Bram.a487b07e_0400_Bram
    <<set $quest_mill to QuestState.Active>>
-> The map speaks for itself. #line:Bram.a487b07e_0500
    Bram: Maps don't speak. People do. #mood:sad #line:Bram.a487b07e_0600_Bram
    <<set $quest_mill to QuestState.Failed>>
<<quest_changed mill>>
===

title: Lio
act: Fair
location: Mill
scenario: Accounts
quest: lio_map
when: $act == Act.Fair
when: $culprit != Culprit.Lio and $quest_lio_map == QuestState.NotStarted
---
<<if $culprit == Culprit.Pell>>
    Lio: They let Pell go. I told Maren it was me, after. She said she knew. #line:Lio.969c4ba0_0100_Lio
<<endif>>
Lio: I made it. My first real map. The stones, the bridge, the river, and the old line, the way grandmother told it. #line:Lio.969c4ba0_0200_Lio
Lio: Take it to the table. It's better than nothing, and maybe better than something. #line:Lio.969c4ba0_0300_Lio
<<give lio_map>>
<<set $quest_lio_map to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed lio_map>>
===

title: Lio
act: All
location: Mill
scenario: Accounts
when: $act == Act.Castle or ($act == Act.Fair and ($culprit == Culprit.Lio or $quest_lio_map != QuestState.NotStarted))
---
<<if $act == Act.Castle>>
    Lio: You were at the castle! Is it true they eat off silver? #line:Lio.6747bd85_0100_Lio
<<elseif $culprit == Culprit.Lio>>
    Lio: Go and draw your border. You know where I'd draw it. #mood:angry #line:Lio.6747bd85_0200_Lio
<<else>>
    Lio: Is my map on the table? Is it? #line:Lio.6747bd85_0300_Lio
<<endif>>
===

title: Corvin
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
when: $act == Act.Fair
---
<<if $offer == Offer.Accepted>>
    Corvin: You have my border. Old ink, brown, not black. Don't disappoint me. #line:Corvin.5b2fcd7c_0100_Corvin
<<elseif $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Helped>>
    Corvin: The cartographer who pulled me out of the dark. I have a map of my own today. I hope you understand. #line:Corvin.5b2fcd7c_0200_Corvin
<<elseif $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Robbed>>
    Corvin: Somebody took my notebook in the mine. You wouldn't know who, I suppose. #mood:angry #line:Corvin.5b2fcd7c_0300_Corvin
<<else>>
    Corvin: Today we see whose map the valley believes. #line:Corvin.5b2fcd7c_0400_Corvin
<<endif>>
===

title: Anselm
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
when: $act == Act.Fair
---
=> Anselm: Prior Anselm, of the abbey. The river has been our border for three hundred years. Rivers do not lie. #line:Anselm.3981de37_0100_Anselm
=> Anselm: Your map will be the fourth one I have seen this year. The other three agreed with whoever paid for them. #line:Anselm.3981de37_0200_Anselm
=> Anselm: They say you went under the hill. What did you find there? Nothing, I hope. <<if $carvings_copied>> #line:Anselm.3981de37_0300_Anselm
===

title: Hearing
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
quest: border
when: $act == Act.Fair and $quest_border == QuestState.Active
---
// The sixth fork and the ending: the border drawn at the hearing, with what the other forks left on the table.
You take the empty chair at the long table. The green goes quiet. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_0100
Ysolde: The cartographer has surveyed the valley at my charge. Let us see the map. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_0200_Ysolde
Anselm: And let us see if it agrees with the river. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_0300_Anselm
<<if $map_incomplete>>
    You unroll your map. [plural value={survey_count()} one="One landmark" other="% landmarks" /], and blank parchment where the rest should be. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_0400
    Anselm: A map with holes is no map. The abbey will not sign this. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_0500_Anselm
    Ysolde: Nor will I. #mood:angry #line:Hearing.54789bdf_0600_Ysolde
    <<set $quest_border to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed border>>
    <<set $outcome to "failed">>
    <<jump Epilogue>>
<<endif>>
<<if $corvin_presents>>
    Corvin: The castle has a map of its own. An old one, from the archive. Please. Look at the line. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_0700_Corvin
    He unrolls a brown, crackling sheet. The border on it runs well inside the abbey's meadows. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_0800
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_mill == QuestState.Active>>
    Bram stands at the edge of the crowd, looking at you. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_0900
    -> Speak for the mill. The road should go around it. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1000
        <<set $spoke_for_mill to true>>
        Ysolde: The mill has ground the valley's bread for a hundred years. Noted. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1100_Ysolde
        <<set $quest_mill to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    -> Say nothing about the mill. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1200
        Bram turns away. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1300
        <<set $quest_mill to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed mill>>
<<endif>>
-> Draw the carved border, from the stones under the hill. <<if $carvings_copied>> #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1400
    <<set $border to Border.Carved>>
    You draw the carved line across the map, from the bridge stone north under the hill to the abbey's well. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1500
    <<if $corvin_presents and $has_proof>>
        <<jump Exposed>>
    <<elseif $corvin_presents and $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Helped>>
        Corvin looks at your line for a long time. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1600
        Corvin: You pulled me out of the dark. I won't call you a liar in front of the valley. The castle withdraws its map. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1700_Corvin
    <<elseif $corvin_presents>>
        Anselm: Two old maps, and two borders. The steward's has the castle's seal. Yours has a cartographer's word. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1800_Anselm
        Anselm: The abbey would rather have the steward's meadows than a ghost's carvings. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_1900_Anselm
        <<set $outcome to "forged">>
        <<jump Epilogue>>
    <<endif>>
    <<if $can_draw_true_border>>
        Anselm: The charter's page says the same. The abbey cannot argue with its own founder's hand. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2000_Anselm
    <<else>>
        Anselm: Carvings in a mine. Well. They are older than the river's last flood, I give you that. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2100_Anselm
    <<endif>>
    <<if $road_around>>
        <<set $outcome to "true_around">>
    <<else>>
        <<set $outcome to "true_through">>
    <<endif>>
-> Draw the steward's border. <<if has_item("false_map")>> #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2200
    <<set $border to Border.Forged>>
    You draw Corvin's line, the one he paid for. Old ink, brown, not black. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2300
    Corvin smiles for the first time in the whole story. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2400
    <<set $outcome to "forged">>
-> Show the proof that the steward's map is forged. <<if $corvin_presents and $has_proof>> #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2500
    <<jump Exposed>>
-> Draw the path the villagers walk, from stone to stone. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2600
    <<set $border to Border.Walked>>
    You draw the line the village walks every spring, beating the bounds from stone to stone. Nobody's, everybody's. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2700
    <<if has_item("lio_map")>>
        You lay Lio's map beside it. The two lines agree almost everywhere. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2800
    <<endif>>
    Anselm: A compromise. I hate compromises. Very well. #line:Hearing.54789bdf_2900_Anselm
    <<set $outcome to "walked">>
<<set $quest_border to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed border>>
<<jump Epilogue>>
===

title: Exposed
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
quest: border
---
<<if has_item("letter")>>
    You lay the steward's letter on the table. "Draw it so, and it is worth forty crowns to you." In his own hand. #line:Exposed_0100
<<else>>
    You lay the steward's notebook on the table, open. The same border, drawn again and again, older-looking each time. #line:Exposed_0200
<<endif>>
The green goes very quiet. #line:Exposed_0300
Ysolde: Corvin. My study. Now. #mood:angry #line:Exposed_0400_Ysolde
Corvin does not go to her study. He goes to the stables. #line:Exposed_0500
<<set $border to Border.Carved>>
<<set $outcome to "exposed">>
<<set $quest_border to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed border>>
<<jump Epilogue>>
===

title: Hearing
act: All
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
when: $quest_border != QuestState.Active
---
The hearing table is empty now. Somebody has left a cup of cider on it. #line:Hearing.0dc6dddd_0100
===
